    "q-213364": {
      "dom_id": "step-q213364",
      "name": "Question 3",
      "problem": "Select the correct options in the reasoning below.\n\nThe integer $17$ \n{{field-1}}\nthe additive inverse of $19$ modulo $36$ since $17+19$ {{field-2}} $(\\text{mod}\\,36).$",
      "worked_solution": "The additive inverse of $19$ modulo $36$ is the integer $0\\le x<36$ such that\n\n$$\nx+19≡0\\,(\\text{mod}\\,36).\n$$\n\nNow, notice that when we add our two numbers, we get a number that is congruent to zero modulo $36:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}17+19 & ≡36 & \\,(\\text{mod}\\,36) \\\\  & ≡0 & \\,(\\text{mod}\\,36)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we conclude the following:\n\nThe integer $17$ $\\text{is}$ the additive inverse of $19$ modulo $36$ since $17+19≡0\\,(\\text{mod}\\,36).$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
