    "q-213374": {
      "dom_id": "step-q213374",
      "name": "Question 4",
      "problem": "Select the correct options in the reasoning below.\n\nThe integer $18$ \n{{field-1}}\nthe additive inverse of $24$ modulo $42$ since $18+24$ {{field-2}} $(\\text{mod}\\,42).$",
      "worked_solution": "The additive inverse of $24$ modulo $42$ is the integer $0\\le x<42$ such that\n\n$$\nx+24≡0\\,(\\text{mod}\\,42).\n$$\n\nNow, notice that when we add our two numbers, we get a number that is congruent to zero modulo $42:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}18+24 & ≡42 & \\,(\\text{mod}\\,42) \\\\  & ≡0 & \\,(\\text{mod}\\,42)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we conclude the following:\n\nThe integer $18$ $\\text{is}$ the additive inverse of $24$ modulo $42$ since $18+24≡0\\,(\\text{mod}\\,42).$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
