    "q-213213": {
      "dom_id": "step-q213213",
      "name": "Question 7",
      "problem": "Expressed as a nonnegative integer smaller than $18,$ the additive inverse of $11$ modulo $18$ is{{field-1}}.",
      "worked_solution": "The additive inverse of $11$ modulo $18$ is the integer $0\\le x<18$ such that\n\n$$\nx+11≡0\\,(\\text{mod}\\,18).\n$$\n\nNotice that $-11+11≡0,$ so $x≡-11\\,(\\text{mod}\\,18).$ To write this in the required form, we use the following sequence of congruences:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & ≡-11 & \\,(\\text{mod}\\,18) \\\\  & ≡0-11 & \\,(\\text{mod}\\,18) \\\\  & ≡18-11 & \\,(\\text{mod}\\,18) \\\\  & ≡7 & \\,(\\text{mod}\\,18)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the additive inverse of the element $11$ modulo $18$ is $7.$\n\nWe can verify this result as follows:\n\n$$\n7+11≡18≡0\\,\\,✓\\,(\\text{mod}\\,18)\n$$\n\n**Note:** The additive inverse of $a$ modulo $n$ is simply the residue of $-a$ modulo $n,$ i.e. $-a\\,\\text{mod}\\,n.$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
