    "q-213391": {
      "dom_id": "step-q213391",
      "name": "Question 8",
      "problem": "Expressed as a nonnegative integer smaller than $42,$ the additive inverse of $29$ modulo $42$ is{{field-1}}.",
      "worked_solution": "The additive inverse of $29$ modulo $42$ is the integer $0\\le x<42$ such that\n\n$$\nx+29≡0\\,(\\text{mod}\\,42).\n$$\n\nNotice that $-29+29≡0,$ so $x≡-29\\,(\\text{mod}\\,32).$ To write this in the required form, we use the following sequence of congruences:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & ≡-29 & \\,(\\text{mod}\\,42) \\\\  & ≡0-29 & \\,(\\text{mod}\\,42) \\\\  & ≡42-29 & \\,(\\text{mod}\\,42) \\\\  & ≡13 & \\,(\\text{mod}\\,42)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the additive inverse of the element $19$ modulo $42$ is $13.$\n\nWe can verify this result as follows:\n\n$$\n13+29≡42≡0\\,\\,✓\\,(\\text{mod}\\,42)\n$$\n\n**Note:** The additive inverse of $a$ modulo $n$ is simply the residue of $-a$ modulo $n,$ i.e. $-a\\,\\text{mod}\\,n.$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
