    "q-213236": {
      "dom_id": "step-q213236",
      "name": "Question 11",
      "problem": "Expressed as a nonnegative integer smaller than $16,$ the additive inverse of $45$ modulo $16$ is{{field-1}}.",
      "worked_solution": "The additive inverse of $45$ modulo $16$ is the integer $0\\le x<16$ such that\n\n$$\nx+45≡0\\,(\\text{mod}\\,16).\n$$\n\nFirst, we note that $45≡13\\,(\\text{mod}\\,16):$ \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}45 & ≡2\\cdot 16+13 & \\,(\\text{mod}\\,16) \\\\  & ≡2\\cdot 0+13 & \\,(\\text{mod}\\,16) \\\\  & ≡13 & \\,(\\text{mod}\\,16)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAlso, note that $-13+13≡0,$ so $x≡-13\\,(\\text{mod}\\,16).$ To write this in the required form, we use the following sequence of congruences:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & ≡-13 & \\,(\\text{mod}\\,16) \\\\  & ≡0-13 & \\,(\\text{mod}\\,16) \\\\  & ≡16-13 & \\,(\\text{mod}\\,16) \\\\  & ≡3 & \\,(\\text{mod}\\,16)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the additive inverse of the element $45$ modulo $16$ is $3.$\n\nWe can verify this result as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}45+3≡48≡3\\cdot 16≡0\\,\\,✓\\,(\\text{mod}\\,16)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n**Note:** In general, the additive inverse of $a$ modulo $n$ is simply the residue of $-a$ modulo $n,$ i.e. $-a\\,\\text{mod}\\,n.$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
