    "q-213332": {
      "dom_id": "step-q213332",
      "name": "Question 13",
      "problem": "Expressed as a nonnegative integer smaller than $11,$ the additive inverse of $22$ modulo $11$ is{{field-1}}.",
      "worked_solution": "The additive inverse of $22$ modulo $11$ is the integer $0\\le x<11$ such that\n\n$$\nx+22≡0\\,(\\text{mod}\\,11).\n$$\n\nFirst, note that $22≡2\\cdot 11≡0\\,(\\text{mod}\\,11),$ and $0+0≡0\\,(\\text{mod}\\,11).$\n\nTherefore, the additive inverse of the element $22$ modulo $11$ is $0.$\n\nWe can verify this result as follows:\n\n$$\n22+0≡2\\cdot 11+0≡2\\cdot 0+0≡0\\,\\,✓\\,(\\text{mod}\\,11)\n$$\n\n**Note:** In general, the additive inverse of $a$ modulo $n$ is simply the residue of $-a$ modulo $n,$ i.e. $-a\\,\\text{mod}\\,n.$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
