    "q-213354": {
      "dom_id": "step-q213354",
      "name": "Question 16",
      "problem": "Expressed as a nonnegative integer smaller than $23,$ the additive inverse of $-49$ modulo $23$ is{{field-1}}.",
      "worked_solution": "The additive inverse of $-49$ modulo $23$ is the integer $0\\le x<23$ such that\n\n$$\nx+(-49)≡0\\,(\\text{mod}\\,23).\n$$\n\nFirst, we note that $-49≡20\\,(\\text{mod}\\,23):$ \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-49 & ≡(-3)\\cdot 23+20 & \\,(\\text{mod}\\,23) \\\\  & ≡(-3)\\cdot 0+20 & \\,(\\text{mod}\\,23) \\\\  & ≡20 & \\,(\\text{mod}\\,23)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAlso, note that $-20+20≡0,$ so $x≡-20\\,(\\text{mod}\\,23).$ To write this in the required form, we use the following sequence of congruences:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & ≡-20 & \\,(\\text{mod}\\,23) \\\\  & ≡0-20 & \\,(\\text{mod}\\,23) \\\\  & ≡23-20 & \\,(\\text{mod}\\,23) \\\\  & ≡3 & \\,(\\text{mod}\\,23)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the additive inverse of the element $-49$ modulo $23$ is $3.$\n\nWe can verify this result as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-49+3≡-46≡(-2)\\cdot 23≡0\\,\\,✓\\,(\\text{mod}\\,23)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n**Note:** In general, the additive inverse of $a$ modulo $n$ is simply the residue of $-a$ modulo $n,$ i.e. $-a\\,\\text{mod}\\,n.$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
