    "q-213351": {
      "dom_id": "step-q213351",
      "name": "Question 17",
      "problem": "Expressed as a nonnegative integer smaller than $19,$ the additive inverse of $-15$ modulo $19$ is{{field-1}}.",
      "worked_solution": "The additive inverse of $-15$ modulo $19$ is the integer $0\\le x<19$ such that\n\n$$\nx+(-15)≡0\\,(\\text{mod}\\,19).\n$$\n\nNotice that $15+(-15)≡0,$ so $x≡15\\,(\\text{mod}\\,19),$ which is already in the required form. \n\nTherefore, the additive inverse of the element $-15$ modulo $19$ is $15.$\n\n**Note:** In general, the additive inverse of $a$ modulo $n$ is simply the residue of $-a$ modulo $n,$ i.e. $-a\\,\\text{mod}\\,n.$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
      "fields": [
        {
          "key": "field-1",
          "type": "blank",
