    "q-213353": {
      "dom_id": "step-q213353",
      "name": "Question 18",
      "problem": "Expressed as a nonnegative integer smaller than $17,$ the additive inverse of $-56$ modulo $17$ is{{field-1}}.",
      "worked_solution": "The additive inverse of $-56$ modulo $17$ is the integer $0\\le x<17$ such that\n\n$$\nx+(-56)≡0\\,(\\text{mod}\\,17).\n$$\n\nFirst, we note that $-56≡12\\,(\\text{mod}\\,17):$ \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-56 & ≡(-4)\\cdot 17+12 & \\,(\\text{mod}\\,17) \\\\  & ≡(-4)\\cdot 0+12 & \\,(\\text{mod}\\,17) \\\\  & ≡12 & \\,(\\text{mod}\\,17)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAlso, note that $-12+12≡0,$ so $x≡-12\\,(\\text{mod}\\,17).$ To write this in the required form, we use the following sequence of congruences:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & ≡-12 & \\,(\\text{mod}\\,17) \\\\  & ≡0-12 & \\,(\\text{mod}\\,17) \\\\  & ≡17-12 & \\,(\\text{mod}\\,17) \\\\  & ≡5 & \\,(\\text{mod}\\,17)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the additive inverse of the element $-56$ modulo $17$ is $5.$\n\nWe can verify this result as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-56+5≡-51≡(-3)\\cdot 17≡0\\,\\,✓\\,(\\text{mod}\\,17)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n**Note:** In general, the additive inverse of $a$ modulo $n$ is simply the residue of $-a$ modulo $n,$ i.e. $-a\\,\\text{mod}\\,n.$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
      "fields": [
        {
          "key": "field-1",
          "type": "blank",
          "dom_id": "freeResponseTextbox-1",
